        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nI need the full history of changes and projections off it. Key-value entity or event sourced?",
          "label": "evals/akka-sdk-key-value-entities/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "3e304803a50c8734927e8af6990274b49b4247cea2e2e209cea68d65819ead49",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "**Event sourced.** A key-value entity stores only current state, so the history is gone, and a View can only project from state snapshots. An event sourced entity keeps every change as an event. You can replay the full history, and Views (or Consumers) can build projections from those events with `@Consume.FromEventSourcedEntity`.\n\nUse a key-value entity only if you don't need history or per-change projections. You can't recover history later if you start with one.\n\nEvent sourcing costs you event schema evolution, since old events stay in the journal forever. Plan for that from the start."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
